  [PASS] V4a  MUTATION CONTROL reproduces independently: the retired kernel is excluded by the banked factors   (max exclusion 41014x; Mars reproduces the banked 33436x to 1.6% and Saturn its 6687x to 0.4%, from an independent implementation.  So the machinery CAN fail and g04's A3a is confirmed.  Note this control does NOT exercise the r-dependence that V3a exposes -- a constant perturbation is precisely the case where the point estimate is exact, which is why the control passed while the estimator mismatch went unflagged)

  V5 -- SCOPE: is the word 'isotropic' load-bearing?  Price the OTHER anomaly in the same currency
  g04's own A5b FAILS: the EFE quadrupole is Q_2 = 3.0e-26 / 3.3e-26 s^-2 against Park+2026's 5.2e-27
  2-sigma ceiling.  Q_2 has units s^-2 and produces a tidal acceleration of order Q_2 * r at radius r.
  Evaluated at Saturn that is a DIRECT competitor to the same per-planet delta-g bound.
     footing    Q2 [s^-2]   Q2*r_Saturn  Saturn dg bound    ratio
   canonical    3.002e-26     4.283e-14        6.974e-15     6.14
         alt    3.269e-26     4.664e-14        6.974e-15     6.69
  [FAIL] V5a  the framework's modified-gravity arm predicts a Saturn anomaly under the ephemeris bound   (IT DOES NOT.  The EFE quadrupole alone gives Q_2*r = 4.28e-14 m/s^2 at Saturn, 6.1x-6.7x the same 7.0e-15 m/s^2 bound that the tail clears by 10^303.  So 'the anomalous acceleration is below every per-planet ephemeris bound' is TRUE ONLY of the isotropic piece and FALSE of the arm's total predicted anomaly.  The word 'isotropic' in the claim is not decoration -- it is the entire content, and g04 itself says so ('the two must never be conflated').  This check exists so that the claim cannot be quoted with that word dropped)

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT OF THE AUDIT
======================================================================================================================

 CONFIRMED.  The kernel algebra, the bound machinery, and the mutation control all reproduce from an
 independent 60-digit implementation (V1a, V4a).  Route A's isotropic tail really is discharged absolutely:
 the smallest self-consistent margin over six planets and both footings is 10^303 (V3c).  No
 measurement now or conceivable touches it.

 REFUTED AS STATED, IN THREE PLACES, NONE OF WHICH FLIPS THE CONCLUSION.
  1. The margin RANGE is wrong.  g04's A2 (and the claim) compares dg evaluated at r = a against a bound
     derived for a CONSTANT radial dg.  Route A's dg is dominated by aphelion, so the point estimate is
     anti-conservative by 17-1522 decades.  Self-consistently the range is
     10^303 to 10^7397, not 10^320 to 10^8900 (V3a, V3b).
  2. '<1%' for the A1a validation is a log/percent conflation; the worst deviation is 1.98% (V2a).
     g04's own text says 'within 3%' and is correct.
  3. 'below every per-planet ephemeris bound' is true only with the word 'isotropic' attached.  The same
     arm's EFE quadrupole is 6.1x-6.7x OVER that very bound at Saturn (V5a).

 WHAT A REFEREE WOULD DO WITH THIS: accept the physics, strike the digits, and insist on the scope word.


